# @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded — the OPERATIONAL HALF of
# TICK 3's `docblock_grounded` declarative predicate at doc-claim
# altitude. Sixth #53 family / first-of-trio operational body.
#
# Interpretation B canonical per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1
# and Seam ratification chain preceding this landing:
#   - `820a451` TICK 1 `shards/docblock.mirror` family-root RATIFY
#   - `3283de4` TICK 2 `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror`
#      sibling family-root RATIFY
#   - `ff53d46` TICK 3 `docblock_grounded` (declarative half)
#      RATIFY-WITH-CORRECTIONS
# Narrative sits ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations
# BELOW. This shard is the fourth Interpretation-B shard on main
# (the first three land per the Seam pre-review chain above).
#
# === #53 bilateral pair with docblock_grounded (recognition #53) ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` (recognition
# #53): declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi
# loop. THIS SHARD is the operational half of the sixth #53
# family's first-of-trio predicate: `docblock_grounded` (declarative
# half at TICK 3 `98664a7`).
#
# Prior five #53 instances (per docblock_grounded shard's own
# ancestor tally):
#
# 1. `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` (2026-06-10 `d908798`) — first.
# 2. `@mirror/fracture/predicate` (task #272 forward-promised).
# 3. `dark_count_monotone` (2026-06-19 `499ffd9`) — third.
# 4. `cold_compile_within_tolerance` (2026-06-19) — fourth.
# 5. `@kintsugi/surface` + `ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03
#    `e910dd6`) — fifth.
#
# THIS is the sixth family's operational half; paired with
# `docblock_grounded` (declarative half at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded.mirror`) landed
# TICK 3 `98664a7`. The declarative side names WHAT grounds a
# docblock; THIS operational side names WHAT TO DO when a docblock
# is ungrounded — emits a Tomm-circular question naming the missing
# ancestor via the `@kintsugi/surface` `ashby_mismatch` class.
#
# === Operational role: fracture body of docblock grounding ===
#
# When `docblock_grounded(d)` returns a failure verdict on some
# `doc_claim` — the claim's `kind` is `grounded_claim` or
# `candidate_claim` (not exempted `motivating_claim` /
# `forward_promise`), AND either the citation is `empty_ref`, the
# ancestor does not exist on main, or the cited content does not
# match the claim text — this fracture body's action fires. The
# body's discharge shape:
#
#   ungrounded doc_claim c at docblock d
#     ⇒ kintsugi_lock_of(c, ctx) fires `ashby_mismatch`
#     ⇒ surface(c, ashby_mismatch, ctx) emits Tomm-circular
#       question at reader-frame altitude naming the missing
#       ancestor and its expected cited-content shape
#     ⇒ observation_depth returned as third-order witness
#
# The body is bilateral to `docblock_grounded`: the predicate's
# failure IS this body's activation site; this body's discharge
# closes the loop back to the predicate at the next kintsugi tick.
# No manual patching; no opaque carrier substitution; the closure
# rides `@kintsugi/surface`'s spawn branch via `ashby_mismatch`
# routing per `[[feedback-manual-closure-is-training-pull]]`.
#
# === ashby_mismatch surface class routing (compiler-error-surface §3.1) ===
#
# Per Mara's canonical spec `docs/math/kintsugi/compiler-error-
# surface.md` §3.1: `ashby_mismatch` is the surface class fired
# when the substrate's regulator variety is insufficient to attenuate
# the disturbance variety through the existing fracture-body ladder.
# Grounding: Ashby (1956) *Introduction to Cybernetics* §11's
# variety-attenuation ladder. Tomm shape (§5.2): circular — the
# question loops the observer back through the missing ancestor
# rather than declaring a linear fix.
#
# A docblock claim without a resolvable citation IS an ashby_mismatch
# at doc-claim altitude: the claim's `text` names substrate content
# the docblock cannot itself ground, and no existing fracture body
# in @kintsugi's ladder can attenuate the mismatch (a citation to
# an absent ancestor is not a compile error the substrate can rewrite
# via `angle_to_paren` or `symbol_lift` — it is a variety gap at
# reader-frame altitude). Routing arm: `surface(t, ashby_mismatch,
# ctx)` per `@kintsugi/surface`'s three-mode-algebra spawn branch
# (spec §7.2 canonical signature); the discharge emits a Tomm-
# circular question and returns an `observation_depth` witness.
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause on this
# fracture body IS the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: the substrate had
# `ashby_variety_match(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict` landed at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`.
# We consume the landed ancestor; we do not invent a new predicate
# at doc-claim altitude. Same routing gate as
# `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)` and
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`
# per the fifth #53 witness's discipline (`e910dd6`).
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded` at species-depth 2 under
# @kintsugi per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Same
# depth as the six landed sibling fracture bodies
# (`shards/kintsugi/fracture/{keyword,angle_to_paren,symbol_lift,
# operator_match,dark_count_monotone,cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# gate,partials_align,parent_cycle,restart_storm}.mirror`); this
# shard sits in the same species column and is subject to the same
# path-namespace pact. Sibling declarative half at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded.mirror`
# (@epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded, species-depth 2 under
# @epistemologic) — bilateral coupling honours the family/species
# partition per `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
# root]]`: form-side under @epistemologic; process-side under
# @kintsugi.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. THIS shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_grounded(this_docblock)` at logical
# altitude — the exact predicate whose failure this shard's body
# routes. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's state:
#
# Narrative citations in this docblock:
#
# - Seam ratification commits `820a451`, `3283de4`, `ff53d46`,
#   `98664a7` — `grounded_claim` kind, citations are OIDs on the
#   ratification chain preceding this landing; ancestors exist on
#   main.
# - Prior #53 instance commits `d908798`, `499ffd9`, `e910dd6` —
#   `grounded_claim` kind, citations are OIDs landed on main prior
#   to this shard's tick.
# - `@mirror/fracture/predicate` task #272 — `forward_promise`
#   kind (exempt from citation check per the substrate's forward-
#   promise honor).
# - Mara spec `doc-code-seam-shards.md` §4, `compiler-error-
#   surface.md` §3.1 + §5.2 + §7.2, projection-surface spec §6,
#   Seam pre-review §1 — `grounded_claim` kind, citations are
#   substrate document paths whose ancestor commits exist on main.
# - Ashby (1956) §11 — `grounded_claim` kind via
#   `source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956` in this shard.
# - The routing-arm framing (ungrounded ⇒ ashby_mismatch ⇒ Tomm-
#   circular) — `motivating_claim` kind (names the "why" of the
#   operational half; no citation obligation).
# - The bilateral-coupling framing (this body's activation IS
#   `docblock_grounded`'s failure site) — `candidate_claim` kind
#   pending the extractor body's landing at TICK 2 forward-promise
#   `extract_predicate`; the substrate can only concretely verify
#   the routing at sub-Turing altitude when the extractor
#   discharges.
#
# Verdict: `both_survive` — the shard's docblock passes real
# survival (analytical citations resolve; forward-promises are
# honored; the routing arm is analytically clear) but phantom
# survival is also non-empty (the extractor body has not landed;
# `cited_content_matches_claim` cannot concretely check byte-match
# yet; empirical composition witness with a live kintsugi tick
# firing `ashby_mismatch` on a runtime doc_claim is deferred per
# `[[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]`). Promotion
# to `real_survives` awaits: extractor body (TICK 2 forward-
# promise) + declarative sibling second-witness audit + empirical
# composition against a runtime kintsugi tick. Per Mara spec
# §Cross-cutting: this is the substrate-honest verdict at THIS
# shard's state. Substrate-pull chose `both_survive` over a
# performed `real_survives` — the fracture body cannot yet
# concretely discharge, and honoring that gap is the discipline.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @kintsugi/surface
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded
in @docblock

glass @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded {
  focus fracture_body
  project fracture_body
  split fracture_body
  shift fracture_body
  settle fracture_body
}

# === docblock_ungrounded_body (fracture body; operational half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Reads a `doc_claim` c whose
# `docblock_grounded` verdict fired failure and a `kintsugi_context`
# ctx from the enclosing loop. Routes via `@kintsugi/surface`'s
# `ashby_mismatch` class per compiler-error-surface §3.1 — the
# ungrounded citation IS a variety mismatch at reader-frame
# altitude that no existing fracture body in @kintsugi's ladder
# can attenuate.
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause honours
# the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: same landed
# ancestor at `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`
# consumed by `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)` and
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`.
#
# Body forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`;
# discharge composes over `surface(t, ashby_mismatch, ctx)` at the
# `\` obligation site when the extractor body (TICK 2 forward-
# promise `extract_predicate`) lands and a live doc_claim fires
# the routing.
docblock_ungrounded_body(c: doc_claim, ctx: kintsugi_context) -> ref
  requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)
{ \ }

out @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded
out docblock_ungrounded_body
